Phasmid: fingerprint inspector

What:     Members listed in bindings/phasmid_fingerprint_allowlist.txt get a
          PhasmidFingerprintTraceScope in their generated callback. With the
          category disabled-by-default-phasmid.fingerprint in a tracing
          session, each call emits an event with the raw arguments, the
          return value, the caller's location, the world and the identity of
          a returned promise, whose settlement emits a matching event. CSS
          media feature evaluations and font family lookups are traced too.
          Off, the cost is one relaxed atomic load per listed call; no page
          script ever runs.
Why:      Shows which surfaces a site reads, in every context, from outside
          the page (CDP Tracing on the browser target).
Profile:  none
Hooks:    third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/scripts/bind_gen/interface.py
          make_phasmid_fingerprint_trace, check_phasmid_fingerprint_allowlist;
          third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/BUILD.gn;
          platform/bindings/phasmid_fingerprint_trace.{h,cc} (new);
          bindings/core/v8/script_promise_resolver.cc
          ResolveOrRejectImmediately; core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc
          MediaQueryEvaluator::EvalFeature; core/css/css_font_selector.cc and
          offscreen_font_selector.cc GetFontData; platform/BUILD.gn
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker, offscreen
Guard:    tests/guards/devtools/fingerprint-trace.py

